@startuml CloudWarehouse_Sequence_Waybill_Dual_Track
title Core Use Case — Waybill Preview Dual-Track Pricing (Class-Level)

actor "Warehouse Admin" as User
participant "index.html\n(Browser)" as UI
participant "BillController" as BC
participant "BillImportService" as BIS
participant "WaybillExcelHelper" as Excel
participant "WeightRounding" as WR
participant "IDualTrackFeeCalculator\n/ DualTrackFeeCalculator" as Dual
participant "PriceRuleCalculateService\n(Payable / Cost)" as CostSvc
participant "CustomerQuoteCalculateService\n(Receivable / Quote)" as QuoteSvc
participant "FeeCalculationEngine" as Fee
participant "IBillingStrategyResolver" as Factory
participant "IBillingStrategy\n(Tier / Overweight)" as Strategy
participant "BillLineTotals" as Totals
database "SQL Server" as DB

User -> UI : select waybill Excel\nclick Preview
UI -> BC : POST /api/Bill/waybill/preview\n(multipart/form-data)
activate BC
BC -> BIS : ProcessImportAsync(stream,\nsaveToDatabase=false)
activate BIS

BIS -> Excel : ReadWaybills(stream)
activate Excel
note right of Excel
  Detect dual-row header
  (账单明细 + 成本明细)
  or standard template
end note
Excel --> BIS : WaybillImportResult\n(+ expected L/X fees if present)
deactivate Excel

BIS -> DB : SELECT Sites, Destinations,\nPriceRules counts,\nCustomers, CustomerAccounts
activate DB
DB --> BIS : master data caches
deactivate DB

loop each WaybillImportRow
  BIS -> BIS : ValidateRow\n(waybillNo, province, weight)
  alt validation fails
    BIS -> BIS : set ErrorMessage\n(e.g. empty province)
  else valid row
    BIS -> WR : RoundForForwardBilling /\nRoundWeight
    WR --> BIS : RoundedWeight
    BIS -> BIS : resolve CustomerId\n(CustomerCode or AccountName)
    BIS -> BIS : ResolveSite\n(ExpressType as SiteCode)
    BIS -> BIS : ResolveDestination\n(prefer dest with price rules)

    BIS -> Dual : CalculateAsync(row)
    activate Dual

    == Payable track (成本 / X column) ==
    Dual -> CostSvc : CalculateAsync(\nSiteId, DestId, RoundedWeight, BillDate)
    activate CostSvc
    CostSvc -> DB : SELECT PriceRules\nWHERE SiteId/DestId\nAND EffectiveDate <= BillDate\nAND (ExpiryDate IS NULL OR >= BillDate)
    activate DB
    DB --> CostSvc : active cost rules
    deactivate DB
    CostSvc -> Fee : Calculate(rules, weight, BillDate)
    activate Fee
    Fee -> Factory : Resolve(BillingContext)
    Factory --> Fee : TierBillingStrategy\nor OverweightBillingStrategy
    Fee -> Strategy : Calculate(context)
    Strategy --> Fee : PriceCalculateResult
    Fee --> CostSvc : payable result
    deactivate Fee
    CostSvc --> Dual : WeightFee + BaseFee
    deactivate CostSvc

    == Receivable track (客户报价 / L column) ==
    Dual -> QuoteSvc : CalculateAsync(\nCustomerId, Province,\nExpressType, weight, BillDate)
    activate QuoteSvc
    QuoteSvc -> DB : SELECT CustomerQuoteRules\nWHERE CustomerId\nAND EffectiveDate <= BillDate\nAND expiry filter
    activate DB
    DB --> QuoteSvc : active quote rules
    deactivate DB
    QuoteSvc -> Fee : Calculate(...)\nvia mapped PriceRules
    activate Fee
    Fee -> Factory : Resolve(BillingContext)
    Fee -> Strategy : Calculate(context)
    Fee --> QuoteSvc : receivable result
    deactivate Fee
    QuoteSvc --> Dual : WeightFee + BaseFee
    deactivate QuoteSvc

    Dual -> Totals : CalcReceivableGrandTotal /\nCalcRemaining /\nApplyComparison(row)
    note right of Totals
      Compare machine fees vs
      Excel L/X expected fees
      (tolerance 0.01)
      → TransitFeeMatched
    end note
    Dual --> BIS : row filled\n(profit + match flags)
    deactivate Dual
  end
end

BIS --> BC : WaybillImportResult\n(matched / mismatch counts)
deactivate BIS
BC --> UI : { success: true, data }
deactivate BC
UI --> User : table: 应收/应付\n机器值 / 表内值\n+ 验证一致/不一致

@enduml

' Presentation (EN, ~3 sentences):
' 1. Preview posts the waybill Excel to BillController → BillImportService; WaybillExcelHelper parses dual-header or standard sheets.
' 2. For each row we round weight, resolve site/customer/destination, then run two fee tracks: PriceRules (payable) and CustomerQuoteRules (receivable), both dated by BillDate and calculated via Strategy Pattern.
' 3. BillLineTotals compares machine results to spreadsheet L/X columns so the UI can show match/mismatch evidence (e.g. 339 consistent).
